The building inspector shall determine if the applicant under this article has made provision for:
(1) Adequate aisles, seats, platforms and poles;
(2) Sufficient exits which are well marked and properly lighted;
(3) Lighted and unobstructed passageways to areas leading away from the structure;
(4) Removal of any pole, rope or other obstruction in any aisle or exit before the structure is to be used as a place of public assembly;
(5) Inspection by a qualified electrician before the opening of each performance to ascertain if any defects exist in the wiring and that provisions are made for immediate correction of any defects which may be found;
(6) Sufficient first aid and fire appliances, to be distributed throughout the structure, with operating personnel who are familiar with the operation of such equipment and who are available and assigned during the use of such structure as a place of assembly;
(7) Sufficient "No Smoking" signs which are visible at all times;
(8) An employee at each entrance who shall require the extinguishing of all cigarettes, cigars and other smoking materials;
(9) Announcement to the persons in the assembly, at frequent intervals, of the fact that smoking within the structure is prohibited;
(10) Proper safeguarding of any use of open flames, or the prohibition of such use;
(11) Clearing of straw, dry grass, sawdust and any combustible trash from the structure before it is opened to the public and arrangements made to keep the areas well serviced where debris may be expected to accumulate, especially under open seats;
(12) Proper facilities for calling the city fire department;
(13) Such special fire equipment of the city to attend such structure during its use as a place of public assembly as the building inspector may decide is necessary for proper fire protection;
(14) Attendance of such special police officers and firefighters as the building inspector may deem necessary for the control of persons in the assembly to prevent overcrowding, obstruction of aisles and exits, and such other control as may be necessary to render the occupation of such structure by the public safe for the public use;
(15) Rendering fireproof the tent and canvas parts of the structure and all combustible decorative materials, including curtains, acoustic materials, streamers, cloth, cotton batting, straw, vines, leaves, trees and moss.
(Code 1976, § 4-20)

